              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": " Carbon is more likely to have the same number of protons and neutrons because stable nuclei of lighter elements generally have equal numbers of protons and neutrons, and stable nuclei of heavier elements generally have more neutrons than protons because the larger number of protons in heavier elements leads to greater proton-proton repulsion force so more neutrons are needed to overcome these repulsions with greater strong nuclear force. "
